  "asr_text": "I try to pick up packages at a delivery office or a locker so I don't cause trouble with redelivery. It's convenient to pick them up when it suits me, but some products can't be sent to a locker, and even if I ask for a package to be sent to a delivery office, it can arrive late, so in the end, I sometimes have to receive it in person. Still, I think it's honestly wrong that I pay the same fee as people who are always out and ask for redelivery, when I'm the one thinking about how to receive my packages and taking the trouble. Redelivery uses the delivery worker's time, so I think it's fine to charge for it. I'd be okay with making the first redelivery free and having people who are repeatedly out pay for it, though maybe that's just my view, since the delivery office is nearby and I can choose how to receive my packages.",
